# Prompt architecture

How the 11 modes' prose SDLC gets assembled, and how a request picks one.

## Two layers

- **`prompts/targets/*/prompts.py`** — 11 mode orchestrators, each a pair of functions (`_build_*_system_prompt` / `_build_*_prompt`) returning that mode's complete prompt text. See [modes/](../modes/) for each one's exact STEP sequence.
- **`prompts/capabilities/*/`** — reusable blocks every target builder imports: `auth`, `kafka`, `pagination`, `linting`, `formatting`, `testing`, `java_testing`, `fix_loop`, `reports`, `deploy`, `api_run`, `infra`, `connectors`, `github_push`, `azuredevops`, `frontend`, `email`, `tools_block`, `versions`, `brownfield_safety`. See [capabilities/](../capabilities/).

## One dispatch source of truth

A single pure function, `resolve_mode_key(github_url, language, framework, python_framework, microservices)`, classifies a request into exactly one of 11 mode keys — matching names used throughout this doc set:

`fastapi_greenfield`, `django_greenfield`, `tornado_greenfield`, `flask_greenfield`, `bottle_greenfield`, `nodejs_greenfield`, `java_greenfield_monolith`, `java_greenfield_microservices`, `python_github`, `java_github`, `nodejs_github`.

| # | Condition | mode_key | Builder pair | Mode doc |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `github_url and language == "python"` | `python_github` | `_build_github_system_prompt` / `_build_github_prompt` | [Python brownfield](../modes/brownfield/01-python.md) |
| 2 | `github_url and language == "java"` | `java_github` | `_build_github_java_system_prompt` / `_build_github_java_prompt` | [Java brownfield](../modes/brownfield/03-java.md) |
| 3 | `github_url and language == "nodejs"` | `nodejs_github` | `_build_github_nodejs_system_prompt` / `_build_github_nodejs_prompt` | [Node.js brownfield](../modes/brownfield/02-nodejs.md) |
| 4 | `language == "java"`, `microservices` | `java_greenfield_microservices` | `_build_java_microservices_system_prompt` / `_build_java_microservices_prompt` | [Java microservices](../modes/greenfield/08-java-microservices.md) |
| 4 | `language == "java"`, else | `java_greenfield_monolith` | `_build_java_system_prompt` / `_build_java_prompt` | [Java monolith](../modes/greenfield/07-java-monolith.md) |
| 5 | `language == "nodejs"` | `nodejs_greenfield` | `_build_nodejs_system_prompt` / `_build_nodejs_prompt` | [Node.js greenfield](../modes/greenfield/06-nodejs.md) |
| 6 | `python_framework == "bottle"` | `bottle_greenfield` | `_build_bottle_system_prompt` / `_build_bottle_prompt` | [Bottle](../modes/greenfield/05-bottle.md) |
| 7 | `python_framework == "flask"` | `flask_greenfield` | `_build_flask_system_prompt` / `_build_flask_prompt` | [Flask](../modes/greenfield/04-flask.md) |
| 8 | else, `framework == "django"` | `django_greenfield` | `_build_django_system_prompt` / `_build_django_prompt` | [Django](../modes/greenfield/02-django.md) |
| 8 | else, `framework == "tornado"` | `tornado_greenfield` | `_build_tornado_system_prompt` / `_build_tornado_prompt` | [Tornado](../modes/greenfield/03-tornado.md) |
| 8 | else, else | `fastapi_greenfield` | `_build_system_prompt` / `_build_prompt` | [FastAPI](../modes/greenfield/01-fastapi.md) (the default) |

The LangSmith `mode` tag and telemetry framework tag are derived from this same `mode_key` — one classification, consumed twice, so the two can't drift apart the way an independently-hand-rolled second chain would. STEP numbers are **not aligned across modes** — greenfield's STEP 11 is "syntax check," brownfield's STEP 11 is "commit changes." Don't assume a STEP number means the same thing in two different mode docs.

## Python brownfield's profile substitution

`python_github`'s builder isn't framework-specific — it serves fastapi/django/flask/bottle/tornado clones through one shared template, parameterized by `_python_framework_profile(web_framework, free_port)`: a flat dict (~15 entries — persona, start command, health paths, ORM block, query-param block, etc.) interpolated throughout. `bottle` falls through this profile to the FastAPI entry (harmless — still Python-shaped). `nodejs` does **not** fall through here — it has its own dedicated builder (see [Node.js brownfield](../modes/brownfield/02-nodejs.md)), because the shared template hardcodes Python mechanics (`pip install`, `pytest`, `.venv`) in ~15 places outside the substitutable profile.

## Deliberately deferred: the unwired orchestrator layer

`prompts/targets/*/orchestrate.py` (`execute()` → `TargetOutput`) plus a `Target`/`dispatch_target`/registry abstraction implement a clean `Target.execute()` pattern that could replace the dispatch above — but the live pipeline never calls it; it dispatches through the `_build_*` functions directly. This layer is exercised only by a standalone dev consistency check, not a real job. **Out of scope for this spec** — wiring it in would mean rewriting the live pipeline's dispatch body itself, a materially larger change than the fixes and consolidations documented here. See [Known Gaps](08-known-gaps.md).
